findings.body:
The PR bumps `crates/tauri/Cargo.toml` to 2.8.3 and the schema `$id` to 2.8.3, and it also updates `cli.js` in `metadata-v2.json` to 2.8.2. The `"tauri"` field in the same file still says 2.8.2, so the file now disagrees with the tauri crate it describes.

::diff{file="crates/tauri-cli/metadata-v2.json" lines="1-10"}

The `cli.js` entry was updated as part of this release, so the `tauri` entry is probably an omission and not an intentional hold-back. If that field is consumed by the CLI or the docs site to pick the latest tauri version, users will see the old release.

::callout{type="warning"}
I haven't checked which tooling reads this file, so confirm its semantics before changing it.

The `homepage = "https://tauri.app/"` line is new in `crates/tauri-bundler/Cargo.toml`. It isn't a version bump, it isn't in the change files, and it isn't in the bundler's CHANGELOG entry. The tauri-cli crate uses `homepage = "https://tauri.app"` (no trailing slash), so the two crates now disagree in form.

::diff{file="crates/tauri-bundler/Cargo.toml" lines="1-15"}

This is harmless at runtime. In a release PR, though, it makes the diff harder to review, and it should either be split into its own change or noted in the changelog.

Three transitive dependency edges moved from windows-sys 0.48.0 and windows-targets 0.48.5 to windows-sys 0.59.0 and windows-targets 0.52.6. These are the `colored`, `libloading` and `winapi-util` crates. None of the change files mentions them, and a version-bump PR shouldn't need them. This looks like a side effect of regenerating the lockfile with a newer resolver or after a `cargo update`, not a deliberate dependency change.

::diff{file="Cargo.lock" lines="1316-1324"}

The lockfile edges are internally consistent (windows-sys 0.59.0 is already used elsewhere), so this isn't a build break. It is still unexplained lockfile churn in a release PR.

`crates/tauri-cli/Cargo.toml` still declares `tauri-bundler = { version = "2.6.0", ... path = "../tauri-bundler" }`, but tauri-bundler is now 2.6.1, and the tauri-cli release notes say it upgraded to `tauri-bundler@2.6.1`. Cargo resolves this because `^2.6.0` matches 2.6.1, so the build works. The published tauri-cli manifest, however, will still say it needs 2.6.0 or later, not the version that was actually released and tested.

::diff{file="crates/tauri-cli/Cargo.toml" lines="1-10"}

The tauri-cli version bump is 2.8.1, and its only dependency change is the bundler upgrade. That upgrade should appear in the manifest requirement too.
